{
  "id": 20,
  "name": "cluster_aware_return_ramp",
  "intent": "Modulate the parent's progress-ramped return weight by cluster_density: when many unvisited cities sit within mean distance (cd high), the return leg from a cluster-internal candidate is unavoidable, so reducing the return_distance penalty prevents premature jumps out of dense regions. Bumping regret by cd forces intra-cluster completion before cluster-exit pivots. Distance remains the dominant grounding term; coefficients stay bounded (return weight in [0.07, 0.5], regret weight in [0.2, 0.5]), preserving the parent's uniform-instance strength while targeting the clustered weakness.",
  "tags": [
    "return_aware",
    "cluster"
  ],
  "code": "def priority(f):\n    d = f['distance']\n    rd = f['return_distance']\n    p = f['progress']\n    reg = f['regret']\n    cd = f['cluster_density']\n    return -d + (0.1 + 0.4 * p) * (1 - 0.3 * cd) * rd + (0.2 + 0.25 * cd + 0.05 * p) * reg",
  "source": "live_llm",
  "parent_id": 8,
  "reference_id": null,
